  "content": {
    "id": "v2-c5fa9-p19-practice-slot-7-upper-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Zoe scored 47 in a Physics test in which the mean was 58.4 and the SD was 9.2.\n\nThe Chemistry test has a mean of 63.5 and an SD of 7.4.\n\nWhat mark would she have to score in Chemistry for her performance to be equivalent? Give your answer to 2 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$54.33$",
      "worked": "1. Calculate the z-score for Physics\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}z_P&=\\frac{x_P-\\mu_P}{\\sigma_P}\\\\z_P&=\\frac{47-58.4}{9.2}\\\\z_P&=-\\frac{57}{46}\\end{aligned}$$\n2. Calculate the equivalent score in Chemistry using the unrounded z-score\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}x_C&=\\mu_C+z_P\\sigma_C\\\\x_C&=63.5-\\frac{57}{46}(7.4)\\\\x_C&\\approx54.33\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
